From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: overby.me <nix@overby.me>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: link CEF framework from CEF_ROOT on macOS

The ascdocumentscore link step looked for the "Chromium Embedded
Framework" under Common/3dParty/cef/${CORE_BUILDS_PLATFORM_PREFIX}/build,
but CORE_BUILDS_PLATFORM_PREFIX is hardcoded to "linux_64" and that
prebuilt layout does not exist on macOS.

Point the framework search path (-F) at ${CEF_ROOT}/Release instead.
CEF_ROOT is the standard CEF binary-distribution root (set by
core/common.cmake's BUILD_DESKTOP path), whose Release/ directory holds
"Chromium Embedded Framework.framework". Quote the whole option so the
literal quotes are not passed through to ld as part of the path.
---
 ChromiumBasedEditors/lib/CMakeLists.txt | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ChromiumBasedEditors/lib/CMakeLists.txt b/ChromiumBasedEditors/lib/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/ChromiumBasedEditors/lib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ChromiumBasedEditors/lib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1142,7 +1142,11 @@ if(WIN32)
         Urlmon OpenGL32 Crypt32 Imm32
     )
 elseif(APPLE)
-    target_link_options(ascdocumentscore PRIVATE -F"${CORE_ROOT_DIR}/Common/3dParty/cef/${CORE_BUILDS_PLATFORM_PREFIX}/build")
+    # CEF framework lives in the CEF binary distribution (CEF_ROOT, set by
+    # core/common.cmake). The legacy path under Common/3dParty/cef does not
+    # exist on macOS (that prefix is hardcoded for Linux). Quote the whole
+    # option so CMake keeps "-F<path>" as a single argument.
+    target_link_options(ascdocumentscore PRIVATE "-F${CEF_ROOT}/Release")
     target_link_libraries(ascdocumentscore PRIVATE
         "-framework Security"
         "-framework AVFoundation"
